<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Bei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">161–223</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Bei was a warlord of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Eastern Han</a> who claimed descent from the Han imperial house. With the strategist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhuge-liang">Zhuge Liang</a> and in alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-quan">Sun Quan</a>, he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a> at Red Cliffs in 208, then took Jing and Yi provinces. In 221 he proclaimed himself emperor of Han, known as Shu Han, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms</a>. His invasion of Wu to avenge <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guan-yu">Guan Yu</a> ended in defeat at Xiaoting, and he died in 223.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liu-bei.jpg" alt="Liu Bei" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yan Liben (閻立本) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liu_Bei_Tang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
